            "rationale": "This simplification rule is the nonmatching-head recurrence of filterAcc, defining the summary by recurring on the tail without changing the accumulator.",
            "source_rule_id": "rule-47fea1538ad0507cb91d9ff53c08576f802ff5036458e5bb1455a1df4a263e0f",
            "start_line": 14,
            "text": "  rule filterAcc(cons(S, REST), PREFIX, ACC) =>\n    filterAcc(REST, PREFIX, ACC)\n    requires startsWith(S, PREFIX) ==Bool false [simplification]"
        },
        {
            "attributes": [],
            "classification": "DEFINITION",
            "end_line": 27,
            "module": "VERIFICATION",
            "normalized_sha256": "95ab8d93624db21de3cda929dad814e59f3f67a33233478cbd9d06222bf7e749",
            "rationale": "This structural helper expands the named proof term loopBody into the exact translated statement list used as the loop body.",
            "source_rule_id": "rule-95ab8d93624db21de3cda929dad814e59f3f67a33233478cbd9d06222bf7e749",
            "start_line": 24,
            "text": "  rule loopBody() =>\n    If(Call(Attribute(Name(\"string\"), \"startswith\"), Name(\"prefix\")),\n       Expr(Call(Attribute(Name(\"result\"), \"append\"), Name(\"string\"))) .Stmts,\n       .Stmts) .Stmts"
        },
        {
            "attributes": [],
            "classification": "DEFINITION",
            "end_line": 35,
            "module": "VERIFICATION",
            "normalized_sha256": "11b0160cb56a842bbc83e22736af7b949ed225b38ba35c6c68f048a2c056b8a0",
            "rationale": "This structural helper expands the named proof term solutionProgram into the exact translated module whose execution is the subject of the end-to-end claim.",
            "source_rule_id": "rule-11b0160cb56a842bbc83e22736af7b949ed225b38ba35c6c68f048a2c056b8a0",
            "start_line": 29,
            "text": "  rule solutionProgram() =>\n    Module(\n      ImportFrom(\"typing\", \"List\", .Strings)\n      FuncDef(\"filter_by_prefix\", Params(\"strings\", \"prefix\", .Strings),\n        Assign(Name(\"result\"), ListExpr())\n        For(Name(\"string\"), Name(\"strings\"), loopBody())\n        Return(Name(\"result\"))))"
        }
